# The self-host image's build context is the repository root (deploy/docker/compose.yaml); send
# only source, never local state or builds. This file sits at the context root on purpose: every
# builder reads it, including the legacy builder Compose falls back to without the buildx plugin.
# Do not add a Dockerfile.dockerignore: only BuildKit reads one, and it then ignores this file.
**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.expo
**/.npm-cache
**/coverage
**/test-results
**/playwright-report
**/.adapter-digests-build-*
**/*.tgz
.git
.local
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example
deploy/docker/.env
deploy/docker/course-files
deploy/docker/backups
deploy/docker/.ops
